  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn [step 6.3](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#obtain-similar-origin-window-agent) we compare `key` with `origin` using equals. `origin` will always be either an opaque or tuple origin, but `key` can also be `site`. The step says equals, and I guess a `site` will always be a different instance than an origin, but when `key` is an origin, don't we want to use [same origin](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#same-origin) in that case?",
